    "long_instructions": "## Store Backup Data\r\n\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Create a local localEvents array and a function to display it. This proves your \"Safety Net\" works before we add the complex internet logic.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Create a const array named `localEvents` with three objects inside (each having `title`, `location_name`, and `start`). Open sample_response.json  and copy real values from three different events instead of making them up.\r\n\r\n2. Create an arrow function named `renderBackup`. Inside, use  .map() to calls `createBackupCard()` once for each event in your array, passing in that event's `title`, `location_name`, and `start`.\r\n\r\n3. Call `renderBackup()` at the bottom of your code. You should see your local events appear on the screen!\r\n\r\n",
